Syntax: innate darkness

A drow racial innate ability that smothers the current room in an
unnatural pall of magical darkness.  This is no mere absence of light
but a created darkness that mundane light sources cannot pierce -
a torch lit within is no help at all.

The darkness blinds every creature in the room that lacks infravision
or true sight, including the drow who summoned it.  Drow themselves
have infravision and so can see normally through their own darkness;
most surface races - humans, elves, ogres - are completely blinded.
Other races with infravision (dwarves, hobbits, gnomes, goblins, and
similar) are likewise unaffected.

The darkness lasts about four real minutes and persists in the room
even after the drow leaves it.  This makes it useful for breaking
engagement and escaping pursuit, since pursuers without infravision
will be left blinded in the room while the drow slips away.

The drow must wait roughly half an hour (about twelve mud hours)
between uses, allowing for approximately two uses per game day.

This ability cannot be used in rooms that are peaceful, warded
against magic, or under permanent magical lighting (temples,
sun-blessed chambers, and certain shrines).  Casting is refused
upfront in such rooms and the cooldown is not consumed.

See 'help innate' for the underlying command.

